[{:db/id -1
 :adr/id "2609070400"
 :adr/doc_type "adr"
 :adr/topic "human-authentication-is-web3-first"
 :adr/title "Web3 first: verified wallet authentication and Passkeys are approved human authentication"
 :adr/status "accepted"
 :adr/date "2026-09-07"
 :adr/deciders ["Jun Kawasaki" "OpenAI Codex"]
 :adr/supersedes ["2608302125"]
 :adr/repos ["com-junkawasaki/root" "network-awai/cloud-itonami"]
 :adr/validation {:gate "root-human-auth-no-downgrade" :green-exit 0 :negative-cases ["password authority" "missing signature verification" "login authorizes transactions" "recovery delay below 48h" "unverified workspace conformance claim"] :negative-exit 1 :missing-input-exit 2 :rule-kaizen-self-test "10 passed" :scope "policy declarations; not live authentication proof"}
 :adr/body "## Context\n\nThe owner approved cloud-itonami PR #610 and explicitly clarified that its wallet login implements Web3 first, rather than a one-off exception. The former Passkey-only rule incorrectly excludes this intended authority. This decision replaces that exclusivity and preserves the other no-downgrade safeguards.\n\n## Decision\n\nSIWE with ERC-191 EOA signatures or ERC-1271 contract signatures is an approved, preferred wallet login family. WebAuthn Passkeys remain approved. Wallet connection and client-supplied addresses never authenticate. Servers verify nonce, exact domain/origin/URI, admitted chain, expiry and signature, consume nonces atomically, and fail closed. Contract-wallet session acceptance checks current authorization on the declared chain. WebAuthn retains RP/Origin binding and user verification. Do not claim equivalent phishing resistance for wallet signing.\n\nLogin grants no transaction, delegated-signing or governance approval. Do not silently link wallet and Passkey principals. Adding an authenticator to an existing identity requires verified owner authority. Recovery remains credential replacement using a one-time offline secret, verifier-only storage, at least 48 hours of server-enforced delay and a fresh approved authenticator, with revocation and no operator bypass. External wallet recovery is not service identity recovery.\n\nEmail, passwords, SMS, SSO and operator override remain prohibited authentication/recovery authority. Legacy closure and source/built/live negative verification requirements remain. A specialized Passkey-only product is allowed, but must not redefine wallet authentication as workspace-wide prohibited.\n\n## Enforcement and migration\n\nSECURITY.md, AGENTS.md, manifest/human-authentication-policy.edn v2 and the murakumo root-human-auth-no-downgrade gate carry the current rule. The gate validates the approved methods and wallet safeguards as well as existing prohibited methods and recovery controls. Inventory conformance concerns verification, not exclusive use of Passkeys. An unknown or migration-gap surface blocks a workspace conformance claim.\n\nCloud Itonami PR #610 (87e4aa5d61bc82b9332aa27c843a5c25b41bdeda) is merged source evidence only. Full build, migrations and live behavior remain pending. This decision does not deploy code, certify all wallet surfaces, or erase prior gaps. Historical ADR-2608302125 text is preserved with a successor pointer.\n"}]
